    },
    {
      "data": {
        "keyword": "Challenge Without Evaluation"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 293,
      "endTime": 688.78,
      "startTime": 678.98,
      "templateId": "KeywordCard"
    },
    {
      "data": {},
      "durationInFrames": 822,
      "endTime": 716.2,
      "startTime": 688.78,
      "templateId": "FaceOnly"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "paragraph": "When people feel evaluated instead of respected, they focus on self-protection rather than growth. This dynamic applies to one-on-one coaching, highlighting the importance of psychological safety.",
        "title": "Psychological Safety and Growth",
        "variant": "paragraph"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 892,
      "endTime": 745.95,
      "startTime": 716.2,
      "templateId": "PostcardParagraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {},
      "durationInFrames": 384,
      "endTime": 758.77,
      "startTime": 745.95,
      "templateId": "FaceOnly"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "definition": "Stands for Status, Certainty, Autonomy, Relatedness, and Fairness. When any of these domains are threatened, the brain's threat response reduces access to reflective thinking.",
        "term": "SCARF Model"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 496,
      "endTime": 775.31,
      "startTime": 758.77,
      "templateId": "DefinitionCard"
    },
    {
      "data": {},
      "durationInFrames": 489,
      "endTime": 791.63,
      "startTime": 775.31,
      "templateId": "FaceOnly"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "paragraph": "Priya was coaching Raphael, a senior manager known for shutting people down in meetings. Feedback showed his behavior was deflating and discouraged open communication.",
        "title": "Case Example: Priya and Raphael",
        "variant": "paragraph"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 1087,
      "endTime": 827.87,
      "startTime": 791.63,
      "templateId": "PostcardParagraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {},
      "durationInFrames": 370,
      "endTime": 840.21,
      "startTime": 827.87,
      "templateId": "FaceOnly"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "definition": "“Honestly, most people’s ideas aren’t worth much unless they’ve really thought them through.”",
        "term": "Raphael's Belief"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 433,
      "endTime": 854.65,
      "startTime": 840.21,
      "templateId": "DefinitionCard"
    },
    {
      "data": {},
      "durationInFrames": 765,
      "endTime": 880.17,
      "startTime": 854.65,
      "templateId": "FaceOnly"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "paragraph": "Instead of confronting Raphael, Priya asked, \"When did you learn that?\" Raphael, surprised, spoke about early jobs and being punished for being wrong. His confident tone softened, revealing a more complex backstory.",
        "title": "Priya's Inquiry: Understanding the Root Cause",
        "variant": "paragraph"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 600,
      "endTime": 900.17,
      "startTime": 880.17,
      "templateId": "PostcardParagraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {},
      "durationInFrames": 753,
      "endTime": 925.27,
      "startTime": 900.17,
      "templateId": "FaceOnly"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "keyword": "Challenging from Respect"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 306,
      "endTime": 935.49,
      "startTime": 925.27,
      "templateId": "KeywordCard"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "layout": "halfscreen",
        "points": [
          "Recall a difficult client, student, or colleague.",
          "Were you able to separate the person from the behavior?",
          "What did that require of you?"
        ],
        "title": "Reflection: Separating Person from Behavior"
      },
      "durationInFrames": 409,
      "endTime": 949.15,
      "startTime": 935.49,
      "templateId": "Takeaways"
    },
    {
      "data": {},
      "durationInFrames": 1067,
